    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22F7UPDYFnmKREEQP9UfNUB)_\n\n## What\nBinary and state files that packages wrote into the config folder (and that were tracked in Git) now live in ignored folders. Full table in the new \"State files\" section of `docs/tangles/base/sp-globals.org`.\n\n| File | Now |\n|---|---|\n| `vulpea.db` (`vulpea-db-location`) | `var/` |\n| `discourse-graphs.db` (`dg-db-file`) | `var/` |\n| `savehist` | `var/` (was set after the mode started, so it kept reading the root copy; now set in `:init`) |\n| `.org-id-locations` | already `var/cache/`, nothing to change |\n| `bookmarks` (`bookmark-default-file`) | `libraries/lambda-user/` (`sp-user-dir`, the existing folder for personal files, tracked by Git: bookmarks are user data) |\n| `projectile-bookmarks.eld` | `var/etc/` (known projects, kept) |\n| `projectile-frecency.eld`, `project.el` list, `amx-items` | `var/cache/` |\n| `org_dataview.db`, `places.eld`, `projects.eld`, `agent-shell/markdown-links.eld` | untracked and ignored (see below) |\n\n## Findings\n- **amx**: `amx-items` held only amx's initial command list and an empty history. Nothing in the config installs or loads amx; the file is a leftover. If a package pulls amx in, its save file is now in `var/cache/`.\n- **`.eld` files** (tracked at the root, all package defaults, none edited by hand): `projectile-bookmarks.eld` (known projects, kept), `projectile-frecency.eld` (visit counts, cache), `projects.eld` and `places.eld` (stale: `nil` and an old `elpa/lambda-themes` path), `agent-shell/markdown-links.eld` (opened links, cache). Already elsewhere: `tabspaces-session.eld`, `fontaine-latest-state.eld`, saved query-table views. User data among them: only the known-projects list and the saved views. No `tangle-hashes.eld` or reload-hash file exists in the repo.\n- **`org_dataview.db`**: an SQLite table of Org properties from the `org-dataview` experiment, which is commented out in `sp-org-ext`. I did not guess its location variable, so it is only untracked and ignored.\n- `forge-database.sqlite` and `url/cookies` are also tracked at the root; left alone.\n\n## Before you pull (Git deletes the tracked copies)\n```sh\ncd ~/.config/emacs-modular && mkdir -p var/etc var/cache\ncp discourse-graphs.db var/discourse-graphs.db\ncp org_dataview.db var/org-dataview.db\ncp savehist var/savehist\ncp projectile-bookmarks.eld var/etc/\ncp projectile-frecency.eld var/cache/\n[ -f vulpea.db ] && mv vulpea.db var/vulpea.db   # untracked, Git does not touch it\n```\n`bookmarks` is moved by Git. If `vulpea.db` is not moved, Vulpea just rebuilds it (slower first start). Nothing is deleted on your machine by me.\n\n## Not tested\nNo Emacs in the container; nothing was byte-compiled or run. The variable `projectile-frecency-file` and the Emacs 31 default names of `places.eld`/`projects.eld` come from no-littering's source and my reading, not from running Emacs.\n\nModule docs, CHANGELOG and the `.gitignore` are updated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiANecP26sDyGKRQbGn)_",
